  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a thin square plate floating on a viscous liquid in a large tank. The height <math><mi>h</mi></math> of the liquid in the tank is much less than the width of the tank. The floating plate is pulled horizontally with a constant velocity <math><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> . Which of the following statements is (are) true?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Df54u",
      "text": "The resistive force of liquid on the plate is inversely proportional to  <math><mi>h</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cdoeD",
      "text": "The resistive force of liquid on the plate is independent of the area of the plate",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DuQwA",
      "text": "The tangential (shear) stress on the floor of the tank increases with <math><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eVRMd",
      "text": "The tangential (shear) stress on the plate varies linearly with the viscosity <math><mi>η</mi></math> of the liquid",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/fskdagvagjyshpoyjmvwwijtttyrmsrrougfkrmoukkcordmvx.jpeg\"/><br >Viscous force is given by <math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>A</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> since h is very small therefore, magnitude of viscous force is given by<br ><math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>A</mi><mfrac><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∆</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br ><math><mo>∴</mo><mi> </mi><mi> </mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi>η</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><mi>F</mi><mo>∝</mo><msub><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>∝</mo><mi>A</mi></math><br >Since plate is moving with constant velocity, same force must be acting on the floor",
    "image": null
  },
